.TH ZIMSPLIT "1" "July 2020" "zim-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zimsplit \- split a ZIM file into smaller parts
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBzimsplit\fR [options] zimfile\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
zimfile
ZIM file to split
.TP
\fB\-o\fR PREFIX
Prefix of output file parts
.TP
\fB\-\-size=\fISIZE\fR
Maximum size of each part. SIZE must be a positive integer, optionally followed
by a decimal unit (KB, MB, GB, TB, PB, or EB) or a binary unit (KiB, MiB, GiB,
TiB, PiB, or EiB). A value without a unit is interpreted as bytes. The default
is 2GiB.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
create ZIM parts even if it is impossible to have all part size smaller than requested
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
print software version

